checkpoint, push, merge,\n22|parent-goal update, sibling spawn or other-Story edit occurred. HEAD remains\n23|`7208cc7427e1ebe95106d34f98214e2bbea4ae1c`; signature verified, exit 0.\n24|Ten changed/new paths are enumerated with hashes in the source manifest.\n25|The source archive and apply-checked patch preserve all work independently of\n26|this headless session. They are partial source artifacts, not a forged CR.\n27|\n28|## Acceptance audit\n29|\n30|**2 of 5 AC rows driven in full at the library boundary; 3 of 5 partially driven.\n31|0 of 5 rows accepted for public CLI delivery.** The unchanged denominator is\n32|selector resolution, ambiguity, list summaries, status summaries, deterministic\n33|sorting. `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md` names every entry, test and bound.\n34|Tests are deliberately uncommitted in this managed Story; no committed-test or\n35|accepted-handoff gate is asserted.\n36|\n37|| AC row | Production entry and named test | Result |\n38|| --- | --- | --- |\n39|| NAME/UUID/qualified resolution | Reader.Resolve/Status; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence; Repository.Resolve/TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID | Partial: NAME/UUID tiers driven; qualified syntax/target/precedence pending. |\n40|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve/Status; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity | Library row driven for local/cross-peer folded collisions; inputs trust upstream identity/configuration owners. |\n41|| List summaries | Reader.List → Repository.ListSessions → Projector.Project; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure | Partial: actual stored/derived facts, no supplemental observation or public-rendering claims. |\n42|| Status summaries | Reader.Status/InspectLocal; same tests plus TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed, TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult | Partial: healthy selectors and explicit local recovery inspection; closed CLI ownership gap remains real. |\n43|| Sorting | Reader.List/Resolve; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity | Library row driven: session ID order, deterministic peer-source tie order, duplicate allowlist/permutation stability. |\n44|\n45|Read calls do not write durable state. The recovery driver interrupts a real\n46|CreateSession after record installation, reads the parked diagnostics, invokes\n47|the byte-identical retry through the repository owner and observes the healed\n48|summary. Repeated list reads prove idempotent read output. It is not a new\n49|mutation/recovery protocol. Projector/record admission remain single-owned.\n50|\n51|Trust bounds: learned repositories and the configuration allowlist are upstream\n52|inputs, not independently authenticated by Reader. No mesh fetch, authentication,\n53|freshness, peer completeness, cross-peer lease union, atomic multi-session\n54|snapshot, safe action planner or public ax invocation is proved. Logical index\n55|eligibility is not process liveness. Source tie order is not ownership election.\n56|No doctor, provider, platform, transport or terminal capability is advertised.\n57|\n58|## Stop-The-Line: exact unresolved dependency and technical bound\n59|\n60|The existing product question remains unanswered: supply the approved\n61|qualified-selector contract, including syntax, whether it targets a source peer\n62|or winning owner, and its precedence/ambiguity rules. v0.5.0 §2.3 and §14.1 do\n63|not define it. The original TASK-260830-21gygk_stop-line.md was reread and retained\n64|on the board; that question is already pending and is not asked again here.\n65|\n66|Options remain: (1) supply an existing approved contract (recommended first),\n67|(2) have the product/spec owner define the missing rule, or (3) explicitly defer\n68|qualification through an authorized scope revision. Option 3 is a scope\n69|reduction and was not selected. No guessed grammar, host-filter default or\n70|qualified-string fixture was introduced. Tests containing @ or / merely probe\n71|ordinary not-found matching, never an approved qualification refusal contract.\n72|\n73|A separate concrete limit prevents claiming full public summaries from current\n74|owners: an event-free valid Session Record projects empty owner, lease and local\n75|role; CLI Result's closed SessionSummary requires a UUID owner, nonempty host\n76|name, positive lease epoch, UUID lease and owner/replica role. The real\n77|Reader.List + cliresult.New driver TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult\n78|reproduces the failure. Inventing values or adding a private wire variant would\n79|contradict the contract. Host display names, checkpoint timestamp/age, workspace\n80|state, provider/platform observations, process liveness and per-peer sync times\n81|also require their authoritative observation integrations. Reader deliberately\n82|preserves only facts current owners can establish. This is an explicit partial\n83|summary bound, not evidence that implementing a renderer is inherently impossible.\n84|The next implementation must obtain those owners' facts and an authoritative\n85|representation/failure path for the unknown-owner case, then drive actual public\n86|list/status output. This run does not expand into runtime-quiescence, upstream\n87|176/177 or other Story ownership to fake those facts.\n88|\n89|No unsuccessful implementation experiment forced a model workaround. The one\n90|initial red test was an invalid event fixture, corrected from the canonical\n91|payload. Full checks then passed; routine rework is not the stop reason.\n92|\n93|## Scoped predecessor evidence\n94|\n95|Authoritative current task reads show both prerequisite tasks `integrating` and\n96|`integrationCheckpointed=true`; statuses were not regressed to manufacture the\n97|literal to-review predicate. The attached/read reducer acceptance JSON identifies\n98|CR-TASK-260830-1r9wrr-3 accepted by RUN-260907-364977 and prerequisite\n99|CR-TASK-260830-wb